ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57, D-93, D-118): filtered layers drawn only within reach of the view
Library: resvg 0.50.0
Fixes: none (speed: a filtered layer cost its whole filter region, linebender/resvg#790 and #1192)
Upstream: none yet: to be proposed to linebender/resvg, linked to #1192 (ours)
Remove when: a resvg release draws a filtered layer only within reach of the canvas, or this patch no longer applies

resvg drew every filtered group over its whole filter region at the scale asked, however little of it
the canvas shows: a part of the canvas cost as much as the whole, and a zoomed-in view its whole area
at that zoom. Here a layer is drawn only within reach of the visible area (render::Context::visible,
taken into a layer's own axes as render_group() takes max_bbox, without the group's rotation and skew):
for a filtered group, the reach of its filters (filter::reach(): the box blur's exact width, offsets,
morphology as resvg rounds its radius, displacement, convolution, lighting); a filter whose result may
depend on its whole region (feTile, feImage, stitched feTurbulence) keeps its whole region, as before.
Groups and layers outside the visible area are not drawn: tiny-skia 0.12 drew a one-row pixmap placed
just above the canvas onto the canvas's first row. A primitive's subregion is cleared within its
result's pixels wherever it lies (it may lie partly or wholly outside a layer drawn in part). The
pixels are those of the whole region but for anti-aliased edges, whose coverage may move by a rounding
step when a layer starts elsewhere (tiny-skia's, as for a shape drawn on a canvas that starts
elsewhere; lighting and convolution, which read an edge's slope, enlarge that step).

